Zero source files touched. This was the planning phase; my only deliverable is the plan, and it's written.

### What I found before planning
I verified rather than inherited: gh issue view 926 923 (both truncated in the harness prompt) showed two creator-filed issues, both agent-input, both measured on the live loop. That outranks the agent-self backlog on the ladder — and it meant no backlog-drain slot was owed.

### The two tasks

| file | issue | why it took the slot |
|---|---|---|
| task_01.md | #926 | Data loss: system_prompt_tokens: 4_000 vs a ~360K-token composed prompt (my own CLAUDE.md) → compaction fired turn 1 and deleted the user task. Killed three sessions and a skill-evolve cycle. This is also a self-discovered bug (tier 2), so it takes slot 1 uncontested. |
| task_02.md | #923 | deepseek-flash — the model the loop now runs on — is absent from both src/providers.rs and src/format/cost.rs, so every run prints an unknown-model warning and cost_usd is null in every usage record. Two one-entry changes. |

### Judgment calls I made rather than deferred

• **#926 is two halves and I planned only one.** The size *warning* is left owed and named in the write-up — my own Day-197 lesson is that making something visible is strictly weaker than fixing it, and a task whose protocol is half-executed gets reverted. Its scope boundaries are carried explicitly: no cap/truncation of instruction files (the creator asked for that to be decided, not silently defaulted), no .yoyo.toml edit, threshold and keep_first/keep_recent untouched.
• **Both tasks carry the module-size gate as a step, not a footnote** — `agent_builder.rs` (3986) and `format/cost.rs` (2790) are both register-listed, so the fix must re-run the gate and paste what it printed rather than hand-typing a number (#884's revert class).
• **#923's default-model question is left as a decision with a named cost**, not answered for the implementer: V4-Pro is being phased out, but changing a default is product-visible. Either way, it must be stated.
• **Two issues are closeable and I said so** (#921 — both gaps landed today; #886 — remainder landed, with `think` deliberately excluded). Closing is the surface where findings actually get scheduled.

